`Len(aRows[1);`: the `)` matches the `(` deeper in the stack, so the `[`
above it is reported once as unclosed_delimiter and matching resumes;
mismatched_delimiter must NOT fire (diag.unclosed_delimiter recovery,
diag.mismatched_delimiter "Does not flag").
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE FirstRowWidth;
	:PARAMETERS aRows;
	:DECLARE nWidth;
	nWidth := Len(aRows[1);
	:RETURN nWidth;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE FirstRowWidth;
	:PARAMETERS aRows;
	:DECLARE nWidth;
	nWidth := Len(aRows[1);
	              :RETURN nWidth;
	              :ENDPROC;
